# Coding Standards

## Scope & diffs

- Minimal, focused changes — no drive-by refactors
- Match existing patterns in the file/module being edited
- Reuse existing services, hooks, and DTOs before creating new ones

## TypeScript

- Strict typing; avoid `any` in new code
- Use Prisma-generated enums (`TicketStatus`, `UserRole`, etc.) — never magic strings
- Validate inputs with class-validator DTOs (backend) or Zod (frontend forms)

## Naming

- Backend modules: `feature/feature.module.ts`, `feature.service.ts`, `feature.controller.ts`
- Frontend hooks: `useTickets`, `useReports` in `src/hooks/`
- Arabic UI labels: add to `frontend/src/lib/constants.ts`

## Git

- Do not commit unless explicitly asked
- Never commit `.env`, credentials, or upload directories
- Use skill `barmijly-commit` when asked to commit

## Testing changes

- Backend: verify affected endpoint in Swagger (`/api/docs`)
- Frontend: check RTL layout, responsiveness, and role-based visibility
- Ticket changes: walk through status flow in `backend/GUIDE.md`
